WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.419 --> 00:00:03.169
(peaceful music)

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.140
- Dubai, for me, is a chance to be a part

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:12.330
of building the foundation for
the underground music scene.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.820
I think all feeling can be felt in music.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.880
I've been diagnosed with
a critical hearing loss,

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.580
so I have really two choices,

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.750
stop making music and the other option is

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:26.260
making music while my ear supports me.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.126
I choose the latter.

00:00:28.126 --> 00:00:30.709
(techno music)

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:45.010
My name is Aaron Kim, aka Tacit.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:49.030
I do sound design and
make electronic music.

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:51.860
I'm from South Korea and
have been living in Dubai

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.160
for nine years now.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.540
I'm, in fact, a cellist,

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:03.250
and I changed my whole
music-making process

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:06.890
with electronic music
because in electronic music

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:08.080
there is no wrong and right.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.010
You don't need to follow any structures.

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:11.880
You are 100% free.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.360
Classical music is very, very strict.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:19.490
What I love about electronic music

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:23.020
is you don't have any rules, any theories,

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.680
nothing to follow.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:28.100
When I need or want, I
go out and record sound

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.710
from the ocean, from the desert,

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:34.010
come back home to my electronic equipment

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:36.950
and I start to make music with the sounds

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:38.900
I recorded earlier.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:42.840
I'm trying to incorporate my cello sound

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.660
in a very unconventional sense.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.340
It's like heavily synthesized,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.160
heavily granulized, chopped up.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.200
I think the very basic
foundations and backbone

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.960
of any city is art and music.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:58.550
There's a lot of people
setting up new things here.

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:00.830
There's a record store called Flip Side

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:03.010
run by my friend Shadi.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:06.090
He was the first guy to open
a record store in Dubai.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:10.430
The underground music
scene is really growing

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.550
in Dubai, and it's new.

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:14.280
Living and creating in Dubai means

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.980
I'm part of growing and
building that scene.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:19.820
So many people here are like me.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:23.070
They've set up home here and
are bringing a little bit

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:25.140
of what's theirs into the city,

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.650
which in turn, I think, is creating

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:29.560
a really strong creative
undercurrent in Dubai.

00:02:31.227 --> 00:02:34.810
(electronic tone chiming)

